      "side": 1,
      "message": "`libspdm_init_connection()` executes `GET_VERSION`,`GET_CAPABILITIES`, and\n`NEGOTIATE_ALGORITHMS` before returning, and `getCertificateDigests()` then\nexecutes `GET_DIGESTS` synchronously. The current libspdm implementation invokes\nthe registered send/receive callbacks inline, and this coroutine has no\nsuspension point before `co_return`. In this transport, the receive callback ultimately performs blocking `recv()`\ncalls while ignoring the supplied timeout. An unresponsive endpoint can\ntherefore block the thread executing this D-Bus method indefinitely.\n\nShould we consider moving the complete transaction to a serialized worker/executor and await its completion, or implement genuinely asynchronous transport I/O?",
      "revId": "f028ba207a6d70be4adb066abcc7b2e76b600d50",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
